  "complexity": 6,
  "title": "Active path 3: handoff-aware executor routing (start strong when expected route cost says so) within pool constraints (v2)",
  "spec": "Today (T-0831) [handoff] mode \"active\" is treated as shadow: executor.start records a \"handoff\" decision with expected_route_cost per eligible executor but launches the baseline pick. Build the active branch. Facts: executor.start picks via pool.pick_executor + allocation (executor.py ~276-323); handoff_scorecard.expected_route_cost(task_class, executor, root, cfg) returns a number or {\"insufficient\": True}; promotion CRITERIA min_samples 20.\nDo:\n1. Active: after the baseline pick, when every eligible executor has sufficient samples for the task's class and the lowest expected_route_cost executor differs from the baseline by more than [handoff] min_gain (new key, default 0.15 = 15% cheaper expected cost-to-accept), launch that executor instead; record the decision row with selected = the chosen executor and reason \"expected_route_cost\" plus the gain; otherwise keep the baseline with reason \"insufficient_evidence\" or \"gain_below_threshold\". Hard pool constraints (eligibility, cooldowns, complexity ceilings such as Astra for \u22659, budgets) stay authoritative: the router only chooses among pool.eligible_executors.\n2. Cap: at most [handoff] max_active_share (default 0.5) of the day's execute launches may deviate from the baseline, so the baseline keeps producing comparison data; count per day in pool_state or the decision log.\n3. Outcome feedback: when a task started under an active handoff decision reaches merged or failed, decision_log.outcome(task, \"handoff\", ...) records rounds, accepted tokens and usd; handoff_scorecard.by_start already aggregates by first executor, add a column \"active_share\".\nTests: tests/test_executor.py::test_active_handoff_switches_executor_when_gain_exceeds_threshold, ::test_active_handoff_keeps_baseline_without_evidence, ::test_active_share_cap_enforced; tests/test_handoff_scorecard.py::test_active_outcome_rows_feed_by_start; docs/context-economy/08-handoffs.md Active section with the revert path ([handoff] mode shadow).\nDo not ask questions; decide and note decisions in the result.\n\nSPEC v2 (2026-09-22 23:05) after spec review T-0851 (request_changes), binding on top of v1:\n- No daemon hook. executor.start stamps `pipeline.handoff` = {\"baseline\", \"selected\", \"switched\": bool, \"gain\", \"reason\", \"ts\"} on the bus task at dispatch (inside bus.locked()). handoff_scorecard.lineage_rows/by_start read that stamp from the task rows they already load: active_share = switched lineages / lineages with a stamp, and outcomes (rounds, accepted tokens, usd, merged/failed) come from the same task and run rows the module already aggregates. orchestrator/daemon.py leaves the scope; no decision_log.outcome call is required (the decision row is written once at dispatch with the final reason).\n- Decision reasons: \"expected_route_cost\" (switched), \"insufficient_evidence\", \"gain_below_threshold\", \"cap_reached\" (evidence and gain justify a switch but the day's active share is full), \"allocation_active\" (see precedence). Tests assert each reason is auditable from the decision row alone.\n- Day counter: computed under bus.locked() from task rows stamped today (pipeline.handoff.switched and ts within the local day) immediately before stamping; the count and the stamp happen in the same locked block, so concurrent dispatchers cannot overshoot max_active_share by more than one.\n- Precedence: baseline = the executor start() is about to launch after the allocation layer (the post-allocation pick). When [allocation] mode is active, handoff never overrides it: it records the decision with reason \"allocation_active\" and keeps the pick. When allocation is shadow or off, handoff may switch. Document this in 08-handoffs.md.\n- tests/test_handoff_scorecard.py::test_active_outcome_rows_feed_by_start is replaced by ::test_active_share_and_outcomes_from_task_stamps (two lineages, one switched; by_start shows active_share 0.5 and the switched lineage's outcome), and tests/test_executor.py gains ::test_handoff_yields_to_active_allocation.",
