  "spec_review_risks": [
    {
      "path": "orchestrator/executor.py",
      "issue": "decision_log.record(\"handoff\", ...) at line 330-336 hardcodes reason=\"shadow: routing unchanged\" regardless of mode. Once active switching is added, this call still fires for both shadow and active (line 323: `if mode in (\"shadow\",\"active\")`) and would log a false reason for switched/gain_below_threshold/cap_reached/allocation_active decisions, since the spec's new decision reasons live only in the pipeline.handoff stamp, not in this existing decision_log call. Spec doesn't say whether to update, repoint, or delete this call.",
      "severity": "med",
      "line": 330
    },
    {
      "path": "orchestrator/executor.py",
      "issue": "notify.notify_once(task_id, \"handoff_active_shadow\", f\"...handoff active is observation-only; routing unchanged\") at line 337-339 becomes false once active mode actually switches executors. docs/context-economy/08-handoffs.md currently states 'The current active value is also observation-only and emits a warning' \u2014 both the notify message and this doc sentence must be replaced, but the spec's acceptance criteria only requires an 'Active section' to be added, not this stale sentence removed.",
      "severity": "med",
      "line": 338
    },
    {
      "path": ".orchestrator/pool.toml",
      "issue": "Spec introduces [handoff] min_gain and max_active_share as 'new keys' but doesn't say whether they must be added to pool.toml with explicit defaults or may live only as code-level .get(...,default) fallbacks. Scope lists pool.toml as touched, so leaving the keys implicit-only would technically satisfy tests but leave the config file undocumented for operators, inconsistent with every other tunable in this file having an inline comment.",
      "severity": "low",
      "line": 354
    }
  ],
